WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.172
Materialization is useful when an expensive result is read repeatedly and consumers can tolerate a known

00:00:08.172 --> 00:00:11.887
refresh lag. The database object alone is not the whole design.

00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:17.927
You also need a refresh schedule, freshness metadata, and a plan for refresh failures.

00:00:17.927 --> 00:00:22.667
Without those, consumers may not know how current the snapshot is.

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:29.262
Connect this idea to a data platform materializing expensive summaries for faster consumption.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:34.622
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.622 --> 00:00:41.862
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.862 --> 00:00:47.712
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.712 --> 00:00:53.200
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
